// # Watch Subsystem Anchor - Change Events
//
// Logline: Reports when a followed file or directory changes, and how it changed.
//
// Setup: Skeleton. watch.oo wraps only oo_sys_inotify_init; the rest is residual.
//
// Beats:
//   1. Detect append, truncate, and replace, and report which one occurred.
//   2. Re-read from offset zero after a truncate instead of seeking forward.
// No implementation yet. This anchor is the documented landing zone for the
// watch pages and gives `make verify` a page to check in this domain.
//
// This domain fills a known hole rather than inventing a mechanism: the add-watch
// and poll paths in std are marked residual. Truncation is the hard case, since a
// rewrite makes the file shorter and a follower that only seeks forward prints
// nothing instead of re-reading from zero.
//
// First page to write: watch_poll.oo over oo_sys_inotify_init, confirming the
// event stream reaches .oo at all before any truncate handling is attempted.
